WEBVTT

00:00:03.778 --> 00:00:11.339
Most of us come to equity work with something real in hand: a
decision to make, a draft to review, a meeting to plan, or a process

00:00:11.339 --> 00:00:13.500
that is not working for someone.

00:00:13.622 --> 00:00:17.567
One DSD People, Access and Culture is built for that moment.

00:00:17.689 --> 00:00:24.451
It is a learning and practice site for staff of the Disability
Services Division at the Minnesota Department of Human Services, and

00:00:24.451 --> 00:00:28.829
it brings learning, practical tools and the right people together in
one place.

00:00:29.396 --> 00:00:33.552
The main menu at the top of every page has five sections.

00:00:33.674 --> 00:00:36.456
Start helps you get oriented.

00:00:36.578 --> 00:00:39.808
Learn holds courses, readings and recordings.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:44.141
Practice is where you work through a real task with a guided
practice.

00:00:44.263 --> 00:00:48.297
Support connects you with answers and with the right person or
office.

00:00:48.419 --> 00:00:53.786
One DSD shows the division itself, its programs, people and plans.

00:00:53.908 --> 00:00:58.720
Beside the menu is a separate link called My work, which belongs to
you alone.

00:00:59.287 --> 00:01:07.227
The Start page opens with three quick questions: the role you are
bringing, the kind of work it is, and how soon you need to act.

00:01:07.349 --> 00:01:14.072
Choose Show me a place to start, and the page suggests a sensible
place to begin and explains why it fits.

00:01:14.194 --> 00:01:18.406
There are no wrong answers, and your choices stay on the page.

00:01:18.528 --> 00:01:22.650
They are not saved, scored or shared with anyone.

00:01:23.217 --> 00:01:30.550
Further down is a part written for people who are new to DSD, and
for anyone with years of experience who wants a fresh look.

00:01:30.672 --> 00:01:37.536
It offers a few ways to get your bearings, including how to use this
site and everyday examples of the program at work.

00:01:37.658 --> 00:01:42.620
Below it, several doors lead into the same program, with no required
order.

00:01:42.742 --> 00:01:50.331
Taking part is voluntary, though existing agency requirements,
including required equity analysis, still apply.

00:01:50.898 --> 00:01:53.838
Learn is where knowledge builds over time.

00:01:53.960 --> 00:02:02.477
If you are unsure where to begin, the Core 15 offers fifteen courses
chosen for disability services work, to take in any order.

00:02:02.599 --> 00:02:10.004
Beyond them sits a self-directed series of seventy-two courses at
Foundation, Intermediate and Advanced levels, along with a

00:02:10.004 --> 00:02:14.366
searchable collection, a library and podcasts with full transcripts.

00:02:14.488 --> 00:02:17.710
You learn at your own pace, and none of it is required.

00:02:18.277 --> 00:02:21.510
Practice turns understanding into useful work.

00:02:21.632 --> 00:02:30.111
Thirteen guided practices are each built around a real task, such as
a decision, a draft, a meeting or a hire, and each comes with a

00:02:30.111 --> 00:02:31.888
checklist you can keep.

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:39.286
For decisions, the page helps you match the depth to the stakes,
from a quick check of about ten minutes to an in-depth review over

00:02:39.286 --> 00:02:40.530
several sessions.

00:02:40.651 --> 00:02:46.463
When policy requires a full equity analysis, a quick check does not
take its place.

00:02:47.030 --> 00:02:50.263
Support is there when you want another perspective.

00:02:50.386 --> 00:02:57.788
One of its doors is Ask, a place to put a question in your own
words, the way you would to a colleague, and get a considered answer

00:02:57.788 --> 00:02:59.897
with its sources and its limits.

00:03:00.019 --> 00:03:02.723
You can follow up or start fresh.

00:03:02.846 --> 00:03:07.323
Please use general or made-up examples and leave out names and case
details.

00:03:07.446 --> 00:03:13.243
When a decision belongs to a person, Ask points you to the person or
office responsible.

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:17.577
The One DSD section shows the division you belong to.

00:03:17.699 --> 00:03:25.466
You can explore DSD programs, services and priorities, see where
equity shows up in everyday division work, and meet colleagues

00:03:25.466 --> 00:03:28.457
through the One DSD Team and Amplify Equity.

00:03:28.579 --> 00:03:36.925
It also keeps the setting clear: DSD sits within the Aging and
Disability Services Administration, and agency policy continues to

00:03:36.925 --> 00:03:38.260
guide decisions.

00:03:38.827 --> 00:03:46.654
Finally, the My work link opens your own workspace, where saved
resources, practice plans, your reflection and the courses you left

00:03:46.654 --> 00:03:49.881
off in are kept on this computer, private to you.

00:03:50.003 --> 00:03:53.859
None of it is sent to your supervisor or to program staff.

00:03:53.981 --> 00:04:00.951
Your learning journey invites you to pick the stage that feels
closest, from Getting oriented to Leading and sustaining.

00:04:01.073 --> 00:04:04.701
These stages are not a ladder, and nothing is graded.

00:04:04.823 --> 00:04:12.158
A good next step is simple: open Start, answer the three questions,
and begin with the work already in front of you.
